
Tunbridge Wells Borough Council
Data Analytics / Business Intelligence Placement

Placement Overview

The placement supports the Head of Digital and Communications in delivering business transformation through better use of data.
Placement opportunities include assisting with the creation, development and maintenance of business intelligence dashboards, following the stages of the data analysis lifecycle:
1.	understanding a business issue or requirement
2.	identifying and collecting data
3.	data cleansing/matching and manipulation.
4.	exploratory analysis and modelling
5.	data model validation
6.	visualisation and presentation
The placement offers the student a chance to work on a wide range of projects both within a team and independently. Whilst the placement is based in Tunbridge Wells the role holder will be able to work remotely, attending the Town Hall when business needs require it. 
The student will regularly work with Digital and IT colleagues and others including service managers and Heads of Service. The placement will also be involved in presenting to Directors, Chief Executives and Councillors.


Key Requirements

Knowledge
•	Educated to A-Level standard of maths or other scientific subject involving numerical or statistical analysis.
•	Have a good understanding of different types of data sources, structures and characteristics
Skills
•	Ability to undertake requirements analysis and planning for data analytics projects
•	Ability to work with others to identify and connect to data sources, following a defined process.
•	Ability to use data visualisation tools (Power BI) to manipulate and display data.
•	Able to produce MS Powerpoint presentations.
•	Able to contribute to reports and provide summaries and interpretations.
•	Able to confidently answer telephone or e-mail enquiries in relation to projects.
•	Enthusiastic, innovative and able to work under his/her own initiative.
•	Proactively raising issues.
Experience
•	Awareness of data visualisation tools and software
•	Good communication and interpersonal skills with the ability to build working relationships
•	Good levels of accuracy and attention to detail with the appreciation for the need for clear organisation of data 
•	Able to summarise information and present it in different formats for a range of audiences 
•	Ability to research concepts / projects with minimal supervision
•	Understanding of the role of information to help improve performance and decision making
•	Experience of data cleansing/matching, data manipulation, analysis and presentation

Key Outputs and Responsibilities

•	Support the Head of Service to deliver business intelligence projects, following the stages of the data analysis lifecycle:
1.	understanding a business issue or requirement
2.	identifying and collecting data
3.	data cleansing/matching and manipulation.
4.	exploratory analysis and modelling
5.	data model validation
6.	visualisation and presentation
•	Use IT skills in technical projects 
•	Assisting in identifying priorities and support key activities 
•	Support the completion of agreed projects

Benefits to students

•	Access to a wide range of officers and experiences across the Council
•	Opportunity to work on and support both small and large scale business intelligence projects and, as experience increases, lead on small scale projects.
•	Opportunity to use skills and expertise to benefit the Council
•	Attend related training courses 

